WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.440
Test 4. This is the IELTS listening test. You will hear a number of different

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:13.000
recordings and you will have to answer questions on what you hear. There will be

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.440
time for you to read the instructions and questions and you will have a chance

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:23.559
to check your work. All the recordings will be played once only.

00:00:23.559 --> 00:00:30.360
The test is in four parts. At the end of the test you will be given 10 minutes to

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:37.959
transfer your answers to the answer sheet. Now turn to part 1.

00:00:40.759 --> 00:00:48.040
Part 1. You will hear a man phoning the owner of a holiday cottage. First you

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.799
have some time to look at questions 1 to 6.

00:01:23.559 --> 00:01:35.040
Hello. Oh hello. I was hoping to speak to Jack Fitzgerald about renting a cottage.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:40.360
I'm his wife Shirley and we own the cottages together so I'm sure I can help

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:46.480
you. Great. My name's Tom. Some friends of ours rented Granary Cottage from you

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:51.519
last year and they thought it was great so my wife and I are hoping to come in

00:01:51.519 --> 00:01:57.879
May for a week. What date did you have in mind? The week beginning the 14th if

00:01:57.879 --> 00:02:06.360
possible. I'll just check. I'm sorry Tom it's already booked that week. It's free

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:12.039
the week beginning the 28th though for seven nights. In fact that's the only

00:02:12.039 --> 00:02:19.360
time you could have it in May. Oh well we could manage that I think. We just need

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:24.759
to change a couple of things. How much would it cost? That's the beginning of

00:02:24.759 --> 00:02:32.600
high season so it'd be £550 for the week. Ah that's a bit more than we

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:40.119
wanted to pay I'm afraid. We've budgeted up to £500 for accommodation. Well we've

00:02:40.119 --> 00:02:44.479
just finished converting another building into a cottage which we're

00:02:44.479 --> 00:02:54.960
calling Cherville Cottage. Sorry what was that again? Cherville. C-H-E-R-V for

00:02:54.960 --> 00:03:02.559
Victor I-L. Oh that's a herb isn't it? That's right. It grows fairly wild around

00:03:02.559 --> 00:03:10.320
here. You could have that for the week you want for £480. Okay so could you

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:15.720
tell me something about it please? Of course. The building was built as a

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:21.279
garage. It's a little smaller than Granary Cottage. So that must sleep two

00:03:21.279 --> 00:03:27.240
people as well. That's right. There's a double bedroom. Does it have a garden? Yes

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:32.559
you get to it from the living room through French doors and we provide two

00:03:32.559 --> 00:03:38.160
deck chairs. We hope to build a patio in the near future but I wouldn't like to

00:03:38.279 --> 00:03:43.759
guarantee it'll be finished by May. Okay. The front door opens onto the old

00:03:43.759 --> 00:03:49.440
farmyard and parking isn't a problem. There's plenty of room at the front for

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:54.960
that. There are some trees and potted plants there.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:04:00.520
Before you hear the rest of the conversation you have some time to look

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:04.119
at questions seven to ten.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.220
you

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:27.320
Now listen and answer questions seven to ten.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:34.279
What about facilities in the cottage? It has standard things like a cooker and

00:04:34.279 --> 00:04:40.839
fridge I presume. In the kitchen area there's a fridge freezer and we've just

00:04:40.839 --> 00:04:48.200
put in an electric cooker. Is there a washing machine? Yes there's also a TV in

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:54.760
the living room which plays DVDs too. The bathroom is too small for a bath so

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:59.679
there's a shower instead. I think a lot of people prefer that nowadays anyway.

00:04:59.679 --> 00:05:04.440
It's more environmentally friendly isn't it? Unless you spend half the day

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:10.239
in it. Exactly. What about heating? It sometimes gets quite cool at that time

00:05:10.239 --> 00:05:15.559
of year. There's central heating and if you want to light a fire there's a stove.

00:05:15.559 --> 00:05:21.959
We can provide all the wood you need for it. It smells so much nicer than coal and

00:05:21.959 --> 00:05:27.600
it makes the room very cozy. We've got one in our own house. That sounds very

00:05:27.679 --> 00:05:33.160
pleasant. Perhaps we should come in the winter to make the most of it. Yes we

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:37.239
find we don't want to go out when we've got the fire burning. There are some

00:05:37.239 --> 00:05:42.480
attractive views from the cottage which I haven't mentioned. There's a famous

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:47.760
stone bridge. It's one of the oldest in the region and you can see it from the

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:53.200
living room. It isn't far away. The bedroom window looks in the opposite

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:58.880
direction and has a lovely view of the hills and the monument at the top. Well

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:05.200
that all sounds perfect. I'd like to book it please. Would you want to deposit? Yes

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:12.720
we ask for 30% to secure your booking so that'll be £144.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:19.200
And when would you like the rest of the money? You're coming in May so the

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:27.679
last day of March please. Fine. Excellent. Could I just take your details so that I can...

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:35.119
That is the end of part one. You now have half a minute to check your answers to

00:06:35.119 --> 00:06:37.640
part one.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.260
you

